Phase 18 API surface audit continuation — 2026-10-22 13:32 UTC

Environment: macOS AArch64, Rust 1.85.0. Workspace branch is `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`; pinned RocketMQ Java source commit is `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`. Kept unrelated Phase 19 working-tree files untouched.

Pinned-source API audit finding:
- The generated Rust `java_encode_with_features` adapter was applied to `CheckRocksdbCqWriteResult`, `AclInfo`, `AclPolicyInfo`, and `AclPolicyEntryInfo`; pinned Java declares these as plain classes and does not inherit `RemotingSerializable.encode(JSONWriter.Feature...)`.
- `TopicConfigAndQueueMapping` also has the writer-feature instance adapter in Rust, but Java extends plain `TopicConfig`.
- `TopicQueueMappingDetail` extends `TopicQueueMappingInfo`, which extends `RemotingSerializable`; its Rust method is valid, but feature serialization currently lacks a root/nested bean schema.
- Other types in the large remoting adapter invocation resolve to pinned `RemotingSerializable` subclasses (or the expected Java alias), so no additional plain-class mismatch was found in that invocation.

Implementation and Java fixture changes are in progress. No Phase 18 plan files or files in the separate pinned Java checkout were changed.

Validation results will be appended after targeted Java/Rust differential checks and the Phase 18 gates.

